robot-browser (3.0.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Replace QtWebKit 5.212 with Qt 6 + QtWebEngine (Chromium 102)
  * Drop the BeagleBone Black armhf target: QtWebEngine cannot run on linuxfb
  * Drop all JS/CSS polyfills — fetch, Object.values/entries, URLSearchParams,
    CSS custom properties, position:sticky and smooth scroll are native in
    Chromium, so the shims and their two-phase injection are gone
  * Replace the hand-rolled cookie jar with a persistent QWebEngineProfile
  * Build with CMake; Debian's Qt 6 ships no aarch64 qmake mkspec
  * Host QtQuick.VirtualKeyboard's InputPanel in-app, since Debian's Qt 6
    QtVirtualKeyboard has no desktop integration compiled in
  * Restore the T420 keyboard: three pages, custom style, touch-sized keys,
    with a toolbar button to show and hide it
  * Add wired network support with its own toolbar icon, and IPv4 settings
    (DHCP or fixed address) shared between wired and wireless
  * Rate-limit WiFi scanning against NetworkManager's LastScan
  * Distinguish the provisioning hotspot from a real uplink
  * Size the toolbar and dialogs for touch
  * Show load progress, and report offline inline rather than in a modal
  * Read settings from /etc/robot-browser/browser.config so the package runs
    standalone; NETWORK_WIFI and NETWORK_LAN select what a terminal offers
  * Do not enable the systemd service on install: session-launched terminals
    would get a second instance fighting for the display

 -- Jan Zwiegers <jan@radicalsystems.co.za>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:21:07 +0000

robot-browser (2.1.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Add NetworkManager D-Bus WiFi configuration UI
  * Add JS/CSS polyfills for QtWebKit 5.212 compatibility
  * Add overlay event filter for QML/QWebView input forwarding
  * Add graceful virtual keyboard loading via QML Loader
  * Rename binary from RBrowser to robot-browser
  * Initial Debian packaging

